ths from 1980 to 1992</article-title><source>British Medical Journal</source><year>1997</year><volume>315</volume><fpage>1205</fpage><lpage>1205</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9393226</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Macfarlane</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Mugford</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Garcia</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Counting the changes in childbirth: trends and gaps in national statistics.</article-title><source>National Perinatal Epidemiology Unit, Radcliffe Infirmary, Oxford</source><year>1995</year></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>ChikeObi</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>David</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Coutinho</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>SY</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Birth weight has increased over a generation</article-title><source>American Journal of Epidemiology</source><year>1996</year><volume>144</volume><fpage>563</fpage><lpage>569</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8797516</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kramer</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Morin</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Platt</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Usher</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>McNamara</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Joseph</surname><given-names>KS</given-names></name><name><surname>Wen<